# Interactive Horizon Builder - starter horizon template
# A flat ring at 15 degrees altitude, one point every 15 degrees of azimuth.
# Purpose: give a brand-new user a valid .hrz to open and edit from scratch.
#
# Format: "azimuth altitude" (degrees), one point per line. Azimuth 0 = North,
# increasing clockwise (E 90, S 180, W 270). Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file somewhere safe (e.g. rename to MyHorizon.hrz).
#   2. In N.I.N.A. > Options > General, set the Horizon file to your copy.
#   3. Restart N.I.N.A. and open the Interactive Horizon Builder panel.
#   4. Drag/place points to trace your real horizon, then Save.
# Edit your copy, not this template.
#
0 15
15 15
30 15
45 15
60 15
75 15
90 15
105 15
120 15
135 15
150 15
165 15
180 15
195 15
210 15
225 15
240 15
255 15
270 15
285 15
300 15
315 15
330 15
345 15
